Subject: [PATCH 07596/11362] [outer-loop] verify node_frame-aliasing fix left
 tu93/HazardMovePruner clean

Follow-up to the arc_solver_kit.py fix: checked whether the same bug
had corrupted the one other cited move_pruner measurement,
HazardMovePruner's tu93 numbers (CLAUDE.md: "states_expanded 2947 ->
2859, -88").

Re-ran both arms post-fix (arc_loop_solve.py --game tu93
--target-level 3, with and without --no-hazard-prune): ON =
states_expanded=2859 (pruned=88), OFF = states_expanded=2947, delta
-88 -- an exact match to the historical numbers in every digit.
tu93's specific measurement was never affected; its search apparently
never hit the failure mode that corrupted lf52's. Closes the
"not yet verified" caveat left by the prior fix with real
verification rather than an assumption.

results/arc_loop_solve_tu93.json (a shared, tracked per-game output)
was restored to its pre-verification content afterward -- these were
verification runs, not a new canonical measurement.

